.git
.DS_Store
# Every env file, at any depth — not just a root-level .env. frontend/.env.local
# was reaching the build context, so `next build` inside the image picked up a
# developer's BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL while Render's clone (where .env.local is
# gitignored) had none. That divergence is what let /dashboard prerender as a
# redirect in production and not here. Examples carry no values and stay.
.env
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
.claude
DockBill
backend/pharmacy-erp
frontend/.next
frontend/.next-build
frontend/node_modules
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
reference-branch
backups
scripts
prompt.txt

# Build context hygiene. Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or
# has no business being shipped to a registry.
**/node_modules
frontend/.turbo
backend/uploads
backend/tmp
docs
deploy/*.md
Architecture.md
*.log
.vscode
.idea
